From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:03:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAESink: pack TrueHD and fill its gaps with empty MAT
 frames

The codec packed TrueHD into MAT frames, and in a gap the sink wrote
IEC pause bursts or zeros. That ends the MAT stream, so an Atmos
receiver shows its notice and mutes at every pause, seek and resume.
Only the sink runs in a pause, and a unit straddles most MAT frames,
so the codec's packer could not end the stream on a unit boundary.
